# Project context
- Farsi-first Pomodoro web app (PWA). Full plan: docs/PLAN.md — read it before large changes.
- The Next.js app lives in `web/`. Run all npm commands from `web/`.
- Stack: Next.js App Router, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, next-intl, Zustand, PostgreSQL + Prisma, Better Auth, Zarinpal.
- The developer knows React but is new to backends and databases: when writing server, database, auth or payment code, add short comments explaining WHY, and summarize what you changed at the end.

# Design
- UI follows docs/DESIGN.md (tokens, components, RTL rules). Mockups: docs/design/source/*.dc.html (phone + desktop). They are mockup files, not app code: rebuild them as React + Tailwind components, copying exact colors, spacing and Farsi copy.
- Colors, radii and fonts come from the Tailwind `@theme` tokens in globals.css; never hard-code hex values in components.
- Every control is at least 44×44px. Use real `<button>`, `<a>`, `<input>` + `<label>` elements.

# i18n & RTL (very important)
- Never hard-code user-facing text. Every string goes through next-intl (`useTranslations` / `getTranslations`) with keys in `web/messages/{fa,en,es,fr,de,ja,ko}.json`. Add keys to ALL locale files; Farsi first.
- Default locale is `fa` (RTL). Others are LTR. Set `dir` on `<html>` from the locale.
- Use Tailwind logical utilities only: `ms-* me-* ps-* pe-* start-* end-* text-start text-end border-s border-e rounded-s rounded-e`. Never `ml-* mr-* pl-* pr-* left-* right-* text-left text-right`.
- Icons that imply direction (arrows, chevrons) must flip in RTL (`rtl:-scale-x-100`).
- Format numbers, durations and dates with `Intl` using the active locale (fa → Persian digits, Jalali calendar via `fa-IR-u-ca-persian`). Never build date strings by hand.

# Timer
- Timer state is timestamps (`startedAt`, `plannedSec`, `pausedAt`, `pausedTotalSec`), never a decrementing counter. Remaining time is always computed from `Date.now()`.

# Data & security
- All database access happens on the server (Server Actions / Route Handlers). Never import Prisma in client components.
- Validate every input on the server with Zod.
- Every query is scoped to the signed-in user's id.
- Pro features are enforced on the server with `requirePro()`, not only hidden in the UI.
- Secrets only in `.env.local` (never committed). Access env vars through one validated module.
- Times are stored in UTC; convert to the user's timezone (default `Asia/Tehran`) for stats and streaks.

# Code style
- Small focused components; colocate feature code under `web/src/features/<feature>/`.
- Prefer Server Components; add `"use client"` only where interactivity is needed.
- No new dependencies without saying why.
- Don't modify files unrelated to the current task.
